@node Transcribe Pipeline
@section The Pipeline

Emacs supervises the pipeline as a bounded parallel pool: @code{cmacs-transcribe-start}
seeds a queue and primes @code{min(jobs, N)} pipelines; each job holds one pool
slot from conversion through transcription (and any summary) until it reaches a
terminal state, at which point the next queued job starts.  The conversion stage
uses @code{make-process} with a process sentinel; the transcription stage uses
@code{cmacs-whisper-transcribe-async}'s completion callback (whisper runs off the
main thread); the summary stage uses @code{cmacs-ai-chat-stream}'s asynchronous
callback.  Nothing blocks Emacs, so the tool is safe to run even when Emacs is
your Wayland compositor under @code{emacs --gowl}.

Killing a job (@kbd{K}) force-removes a running conversion container (as
@code{cmacs-transcode} does), cancels an in-flight summary stream, and lets an
in-progress whisper inference finish but discards its result.

@node Transcribe Outputs
@section Outputs and Naming

@table @file
@item <input>.txt
The plain transcript (always).  With @code{cmacs-transcribe-naming} = @code{append}
(default), @file{talk.mp4} @result{} @file{talk.mp4.txt}; with @code{base} it is
@file{talk.txt}.
@item <input>.org
The summary document (when summaries are on): sections @code{* Summary},
@code{* Metadata}, and @code{* Transcript} (the full transcript, last).
@item <input>.srt / .vtt / .ts.txt
Optional subtitle / timestamped transcripts built from whisper's segment
timings.  Enable with @kbd{f} or the @code{cmacs-transcribe-emit-*} customs.
Subtitles default to @emph{base} naming (@file{talk.srt}) so video players
auto-load them.
@end table

By default every output is a sidecar next to its input.  Set
@code{cmacs-transcribe-output-dir} (@kbd{o}) to collect transcripts elsewhere,
and @code{cmacs-transcribe-summary-dir} (@kbd{O}) to file summary documents into a
notes / PARA repository independently.

Once a file is done its queue line becomes a button: press @kbd{v} (or click it
with @kbd{mouse-2}) to open the @file{.txt} transcript, and @kbd{V} to open the
@file{.org} summary if one exists.  If you ran the queue with summaries off, put
point on a finished line and press @kbd{r}
(@code{cmacs-transcribe-summarize-at-point}) to summarise just that file after the
fact --- it streams a summary and writes the @file{.org} without re-transcribing.

@node Transcribe Summaries
@section Summaries

When @option{--with-cmacs-ai} is built and a provider is configured, press
@kbd{s} to enable summaries and @kbd{S} to pick a @emph{content-type template}
(@code{cmacs-transcribe-summary-templates}: @code{general}, @code{meeting},
@code{lecture}, @code{interview}, @code{research}, @code{podcast}, @dots{}).
Add your own by extending the alist.  Summaries stream asynchronously, so they
never block Emacs; if a summary fails the job still completes with its
@file{.txt}.

@node Transcribe Hooks
@section Hooks: Integrate With Anything

Two abnormal hooks route every result wherever a user config likes:

@vtable @code
@item cmacs-transcribe-after-transcription-functions
Run after @file{<input>.txt} is written, before summarising.
@item cmacs-transcribe-after-summary-functions
Run after the summary @file{.org} is written (adds @code{:summary} and
@code{:org-file}).
@end vtable

Each is called with a single INFO plist: @code{:input-file}, @code{:kind},
@code{:text-file}, @code{:org-file}, @code{:srt-file}, @code{:vtt-file},
@code{:ts-file}, @code{:text}, @code{:segments}, @code{:summary},
@code{:summary-type}, @code{:duration-seconds}, @code{:file-hash} (SHA-256),
@code{:model}, @code{:language}, @code{:threads}, @code{:type}, @code{:tags},
@code{:source}, and @code{:transcribed-at} (ISO-8601).  This is a superset of
what a transcription database typically stores, so a hook can insert a row with
no cmacs-side coupling.  See the org guide's reference for a copy-paste
PostgreSQL example.

@node Transcribe Options
@section Options

All options live in the @code{cmacs-transcribe} customize group.  The ffmpeg
@emph{backend} is not re-declared here: the conversion pre-pass reuses
@code{cmacs-transcode}'s backend settings (@code{cmacs-transcode-backend},
@code{cmacs-transcode-container-image}, and the
@env{CMACS_TRANSCODE_CONTAINER_RUNTIME} environment variable).

@vtable @code
@item cmacs-transcribe-parallel-jobs
Files in the pipeline at once.  Default @code{1}.
@item cmacs-transcribe-threads
CPU cores per whisper transcription (nil = all cores).  Default @code{4}.
@item cmacs-transcribe-poll-interval
Seconds between live redraws (nil/0 disables the timer).  Default @code{2}.
@item cmacs-transcribe-max-retries
Attempts for the ffmpeg conversion stage.  Default @code{2}.
@item cmacs-transcribe-process-filter
@code{missing} / @code{existing} / nil, keyed on the @file{.txt} file.
@item cmacs-transcribe-model
Whisper model basename (nil = @code{cmacs-whisper-default-model}).
@item cmacs-transcribe-language
2-letter code (nil = @code{cmacs-whisper-language}).
@item cmacs-transcribe-output-dir
Transcript output directory (nil = sidecar).
@item cmacs-transcribe-summary-dir
Summary Org directory (nil = follow @code{cmacs-transcribe-output-dir}).
@item cmacs-transcribe-naming
@code{append} (@file{talk.mp4.txt}) or @code{base} (@file{talk.txt}).
@item cmacs-transcribe-subtitle-naming
Naming for @file{.srt}/@file{.vtt}.  Default @code{base}.
@item cmacs-transcribe-emit-srt
@itemx cmacs-transcribe-emit-vtt
@itemx cmacs-transcribe-emit-timestamped-txt
Enable the extra subtitle / timestamped outputs.
@item cmacs-transcribe-summarize
Summarise each transcript into an Org file.  Default nil.
@item cmacs-transcribe-summary-type
Active summary template key.  Default @code{general}.
@item cmacs-transcribe-summary-templates
Alist of TYPE @result{} system prompt.
@item cmacs-transcribe-summary-provider
@itemx cmacs-transcribe-summary-model
Provider / model for summaries (nil = cmacs-ai defaults).
@item cmacs-transcribe-source
@itemx cmacs-transcribe-type
@itemx cmacs-transcribe-tags
Metadata copied into the hook INFO plist.
@item cmacs-transcribe-compute-file-hash
@itemx cmacs-transcribe-sha256-program
Whether and how to compute the per-input SHA-256 for @code{:file-hash}.
@item cmacs-transcribe-ffmpeg-extra-args
Extra ffmpeg args inserted into the audio-extraction command.
@end vtable

@node Transcribe Examples
@section Examples

@itemize @bullet
@item
@strong{Transcribe a folder of recordings} --- Dired, mark them, @kbd{M-x
cmacs-transcribe}, @key{RET}.
@item
@strong{Meeting notes with action items} --- press @kbd{s}, then @kbd{S}
@result{} @code{meeting}, then @key{RET}; read @file{<file>.org}.
@item
@strong{Subtitles for a video} --- press @kbd{f} until @samp{extra:srt}, then
@key{RET}; @file{talk.srt} lands next to @file{talk.mp4}.
@item
@strong{Summaries into your notes} --- press @kbd{O} and choose your PARA inbox.
@item
@strong{Programmatically} ---
@code{(cmacs-transcribe-file "~/rec/standup.m4a" :summarize t :summary-type 'meeting)}.
@end itemize
